From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, win32u, user32, server: a touch is a touch; a pen plugged in later, a pen leaving range

Touches reached Windows programs only as the mouse (0783: the X server
moved and clicked the pointer for the first finger; 1001 made two fingers
the wheel in the shell for any window). No program could tell a touch
from the mouse: Chromium's, Qt's and the like's touch support never woke
(GetSystemMetrics(SM_DIGITIZER) said no touch screen, GetPointerTouchInfo
failed), a second finger was nothing to them, and a two-finger scroll
starting over a button clicked it (the first finger had pressed it).
Before 0783, Wine had asked for touches, but its touch messages named no
window and went nowhere -- windows could not be chosen or dragged.

Now, as on Windows:
- winex11 takes the touch screens' touches on its windows (XI2 touch
  events; a Linux program's window inside ours is deeper and asks for
  the pointer itself, so its touches stay the X server's clicks), each a
  WM_POINTERDOWN/UPDATE/UP of PT_TOUCH to the window it went down on --
  win32u picks the child window under it -- with GetPointerType,
  GetPointerInfo, GetPointerTouchInfo(-History) and the frame of every
  finger down (GetPointerFrameTouchInfo(-History), GetPointerFrameInfo).
  GetPointerDevices lists the touch screen, SM_DIGITIZER and
  SM_MAXIMUMTOUCHES name it. A touch on a program in the background
  brings it to the front (WM_POINTERACTIVATE; not a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE
  window).
- The server makes the first touch the mouse too, marked as Windows marks
  it (GetMessageExtraInfo 0xff515780 and the pointer id), and win32u
  drops those mouse messages for a window that took the touch's
  WM_POINTERDOWN itself (it never reached DefWindowProc; user32 now
  dispatches WM_POINTERDOWN through win32u to see that). The button does
  not go down with the finger: when it moves (a drag), stays still 200 ms
  (press and hold) or lifts (a tap: down and up at once); a second finger
  first, and it never does -- a scroll or pinch starting over a button no
  longer clicks it. A touch from the left or right edge moving in is the
  shell's swipe, not a drag.
- DefWindowProc of a touch's pointer messages gives WM_TOUCH to a window
  registered with RegisterTouchWindow (GetTouchInputInfo, IsTouchWindow,
  UnregisterTouchWindow) and WM_GESTURE to the others (GetGestureInfo,
  Get/SetGestureConfig): two fingers moving together pan, spreading or
  closing zoom; DefWindowProc of WM_GESTURE is the mouse wheel (the page
  follows the fingers, sideways the horizontal wheel) and Ctrl+wheel for
  a zoom -- waiting until Ctrl is down, which the shell's keyboard hook
  held back, and no more after the gesture ended (its end had no
  distance and zoomed out for ever).
- Wine grabbed the pointer for a move or a menu while a touch was down
  (Wine's move loop, a window dragged by a touch); the grab took the rest
  of the touch, its end never came, and the touch stayed down for ever.
  No grab while touches are down on the thread's windows.
- The desktop's thread takes the touch screens' raw events for the edges
  only: a swipe in from the right edge is Win+A (the notification
  centre), from the left Win+Tab (Task View), as on a tablet.
- Every touch going down is stamped on the desktop window
  (__wine_sg_touch_time, and the window in __wine_sg_touch_hwnd), for
  sg-shell's touch keyboard, which shows itself for a text field focused
  by a touch.

Pens (1000):
- A pen first seen after a program started reached no program: the
  devices were read once per process. XI_HierarchyChanged now reads them
  again, and each thread's windows take the new pens' events.
- A pen lifted out of range sent nothing: Xwayland's pens have no
  proximity events. sg-compositor 0.2.0+sg40 says it on the root window
  (_SG_PEN_IN_RANGE); the desktop's thread sends WM_POINTERLEAVE without
  POINTER_FLAG_INRANGE, and the server now delivers a driver's leave (it
  only forgot the pen).
- A pen in the screen's lower half had its state spoiled: MAKELONG is
  signed and y >= 32768 of 65535 sign-extended into the pressure, tilt and
  eraser bits.

Test: test/touch-gate.sh with test/touch-probe.c and sg-compositor's
-Dtest-tablet build (0.2.0+sg40): a program taking touches, one registered
for WM_TOUCH, one leaving them to DefWindowProc in the shell's desktop
(tap, drag-select, title bar drag, two-finger scroll over a button,
sideways pan, pinch, activation), edge swipes, a pen plugged in late, out
of range and in the lower half; test/pentouch-gate.sh still passes (its
probe leaves touches to DefWindowProc now). Mutants, each failing it:
SG_MUTANT_NO_TOUCH_POINTER, NO_PEN_HOTPLUG, NO_PEN_LEAVE, NO_EDGE_SWIPE,
PEN_SIGNED_LPARAM (winex11 mouse.c), TOUCH_GRAB (winex11 window.c),
NO_TOUCH_PROMOTE, TOUCH_PRESS_AT_ONCE, NO_PEN_LEAVE_QUEUED (server
queue.c), NO_TOUCH_INFO (win32u message.c), TOUCH_MOUSE_ALWAYS,
NO_GESTURE, NO_TOUCH_ACTIVATE, NO_CTRL_WAIT, GESTURE_END_WHEEL (win32u
input.c), NO_WM_TOUCH (user32 input.c), POINTERDOWN_UNWINDABLE (user32
message.c).
